# The ending underneath_the_crooked_moon (data/endings/underneath_the_crooked_moon.json): the narration the ending screen plays before its slides. The Vagrant tells it
# afterwards: second person, present tense, one or two sentences a line, no game words. First draft by Claude; Gemini edits it.

~ start
Narrator: The last offering settles on the goat skull, and the moon draws a long breath and pulls the Crooked Queen up into itself like a tide going out.
Narrator: The Crooked Tree catches from the roots up, and you stand in the heat of it and watch a god's prison burn to the ground.
Narrator: You walk back through the Wytchwood with the fire at your backs, and nothing in the dark so much as rustles at you.
Narrator: Days later, down at the old platform, a whistle comes out of the mist, long and low and glad.
the_vagrant: Well now, look at y'all. Tickets, please. I believe this one's the ride home.
